sparky-stereo-browser (@DEBVERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Where the browser draws its window without the graphics card (its own
    compositor in software: a computer or virtual machine without 3D, a
    blocked driver), the 3D Canvas camera and the flat WebXR display still
    reach the desktop in 3D: the page's two views are declared to Stereo
    KWin as one full side-by-side picture on the canvas's own surface,
    through shared memory. Before, both views were shown squeezed side by
    side in the canvas's place, the same in each eye. Pages without 3D and
    the hardware route are unchanged.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@
